{
    "background_story": "Athena was a tiny, yet fierce, biting midge from the family Ceratopogonidae. She lived in a dense, humid forest where her kind thrived. Athena's life was a constant struggle for survival, as she navigated the dangers of the forest floor and avoided the snapping jaws of hungry spiders. Despite her small size, she was a formidable hunter, using her sharp mouthparts to feed on the blood of unsuspecting animals. Athena's claim to fame came when she became the unlikely heroine of the forest, helping to pollinate the rare and exotic flowers that bloomed only under the light of the full moon. Her unique relationship with these flowers earned her a special place in the forest ecosystem, and she was revered by the other insects as a tiny, but mighty, force of nature.",
